# Testing

- Runner is Vitest via `npm test`. Colocate tests as `*.test.ts` next to the source.
- RED first: write the failing test, watch it fail, then implement the minimum to go green.
- One behavior per test. Descriptive names: `returns empty array when no profiles match`.
- No shared mutable state between tests. Arrange-Act-Assert. No `setTimeout` assertions.
- Cover edge cases: empty input, invalid input, missing key, boundary values, error paths.
- Mock at boundaries: Supabase clients and Meta API calls. Never hit real services in unit tests.
- Use `demo`-marked fixtures for synthetic data. Never invent real-looking rows or model text.
- Test user-visible behavior (roles, labels, text) over internals. No snapshot tests for components.
- Targets: 80% standard, 100% auth and secrets handling, 90% pure utils, 70% UI containers.
- Fix the implementation, not the test, unless the test itself is wrong.
